# Everything here is read by FreeBSD, and the compiled stylesheets are compared byte for byte with
# what the sources compile to: a CRLF checkout must not reach either.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary

# What an appliance carries is the archive of a commit: the tarball the self-update downloads, and
# what xgs-image-builder puts into an image (its fetch-project.sh takes `git archive`). Nothing an
# appliance does not read goes into it: the documentation and its pictures, the workflows, the files
# about the project itself, and the repository's own tools, which run from a checkout here and in
# CI (2026-10-22). A file an appliance starts to read leaves this list in the same change.
# package.json and its lock are the stylesheet compiler's, run here; an appliance takes the
# compiled stylesheets under src/. THIRD-PARTY.md goes with the fonts it covers.
docs/ export-ignore
.github/ export-ignore
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md export-ignore
CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
SECURITY.md export-ignore
tools/ export-ignore
package.json export-ignore
package-lock.json export-ignore
# README.md is left out too since 2026-10-30: nothing on an appliance reads it, and an image kept it
# beside the code (measured on an XGS 3300). LICENSE and THIRD-PARTY.md stay, the terms the code
# and its fonts are given under.
/README.md export-ignore
